# Trivy ignore file
# Document the rationale for each suppressed finding.
#
# Read by the image scans in .github/workflows/trivy-images.yaml (weekly) and the release gate in
# .github/workflows/publish-images.yaml. They only report fixable HIGH and CRITICAL findings, so
# add an ID only for one of those that does not apply to us, with the reason and a review date.

# CVE-2023-54404 (zod: denial of service through unbounded array validation, fixed only in zod 4.6.6). The zod 3.25.76
# that Trivy finds in the web, space and live images is not used by the apps: its only dependent is
# react-doctor > eslint-plugin-react-hooks, a root devDependency (a lint tool), whose files end up in the images'
# pnpm store but are never loaded. The runtime zod is 4.6.7. Review by 2026-11-30, or drop this entry once
# react-doctor moves to zod 4.
CVE-2023-54404
#
# History: CVE-2026-30242 (SSRF in Plane's webhook URL serializer) used to be listed here because Trivy
# matched our backend's distribution name "Plane" and its old pyproject.toml version (0.24.0) against
# the makeplane/plane advisory ("fixed in 1.2.3"). pyproject.toml now carries the repo release version
# (1.3.1+pi.2), and a Trivy Images run on the published pi-plane-api image without the entry did not
# report it, so it was removed. The SSRF mitigation itself lives in plane/utils/url_security.py and
# plane/utils/ip_address.py.
